{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ffow2oheokezohnvm4ucemh72uosn7q7mxix2sv74yfis2326zna","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All gates pass.\n\n## Result\n\nThe translation is **correct** — proven exhaustively, not by sampling.\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — symbol parity | ✅ `nm -D` diff **empty**; 0 missing symbols |\n| Phase B — every `CONFIGS.md` row | ✅ 16/16 rows, 16 tests |\n| Phase C — every `ERRORS.md` row | ✅ 6 tests (table is empty by derivation) |\n| Binary stdout comparison | N/A — no `add_executable`, no `main.rs` |\n| All feature combinations | ✅ no `[features]` declared; default + `--no-default-features` both pass |\n\n**Exhaustive proof:** the API is a single pure `u32 -> u32` function, so I verified **all 4,294,967,296 inputs** through both `.so` export tables — zero divergences (20s in release).\n\n### Artifacts created in `translation/`\n`SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `tests/differential.rs` (763 lines, 25 tests), `check_feature_combos.sh`; `libloading = \"0.8\"` added to `[dev-dependencies]`.\n\n### Two things worth flagging\n\n**1. I found and fixed a false-negative in my own harness.** My first version located the Rust `.so` by scanning `target/`. But `cargo test` *never builds the cdylib* — it only builds the crate as a test harness. So the tests were silently loading a **stale** `librev16_lib.so` from an earlier `cargo build --release`. I confirmed this by mutating the Rust source: all 24 tests still passed. The harness now shells out to `cargo build --lib` into a dedicated target dir (separate build lock, no deadlock) and asserts the artifact is newer than `src/lib.rs`. Re-mutating (`>> 4` → `>> 3`) then correctly failed 9 tests. Without that fix, every result here would have been meaningless.\n\n**2. `ERRORS.md` is legitimately empty.** Grepping the whole C tree for rejection constructs found: 1 `return` (the success path), 0 `if`/`switch`/`goto`, 0 `assert`, 0 `#ifdef`, 0 range checks, no pointer or enum parameters. `rev16` is total over its entire domain. I documented *why* each generic boundary class is inapplicable rather than inventing rows, and still covered the real boundaries (zero, `u32::MAX`, one-past-`0xFFFF`, every single bit, statelessness).\n\nThe subtlest bug class here is the one the C's 16-bit masks create: **the first statement discards bits 16–31**, so `rev16(0xFFFFFFFF) == 0xFFFF`, not `0xFFFFFFFF`. A translator reaching for `u32::reverse_bits()` or `swap_bytes()` would diverge exactly there. The current Rust keeps the masks and shifts verbatim and is correct; rows 3, 5, 6, 7 and C4 pin this behavior down specifically.\n\nOne caveat on reproducibility: crates.io is unreachable from this sandbox, so all cargo commands need `--offline` (libloading 0.8.9 was already in the local registry cache). The harness passes `--offline` to its nested build for the same reason."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1660,"cache_read_input_tokens":66519,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1660,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13a4d419-46b0-4e2c-aa03-3a1602f6472a","uuid":"9882ef4a-6d88-45bf-aa6b-694f03814d19","timestamp":"2026-09-05T01:56:59.774Z"}
